+## How a run works
+- Nothing starts at power-up. Press **B1 (down)** or **B2 (up)** to set the target (20-50 °C, 1 °C per press);
+  each press starts a run toward the target shown on the OLED.
+- The Peltier runs at **full power** (`TEC_MAX_DUTY`) until the water reaches the target, then the Peltier and
+  fan switch off and the OLED shows **REACHED**. It stays off, even if the temperature drifts afterwards,
+  until the next button press.
+- To run again toward the same target, press **B2 then B1** (or the reverse) so the target ends where it was.
+- Reversing hot to cold (or the other way) still waits `REVERSE_COOLDOWN_MS` (60 s) with the Peltier off; the OLED shows `WAIT`.
+- Over-temperature, under-temperature, sensor and fan-stall faults are unchanged.
+
 ## Wiring notes
 - DS18B20 DATA (GPIO14): 4.7 kΩ pull-up to 3.3 V.
 - SUNON tach (GPIO34): input-only pin with no internal pull-up, so add 10 kΩ to 3.3 V
